+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially replacing SMS with email to save money.
+Reminders help members collect their pantry orders; they go by SMS because an email trial saw more missed pickups
+and fresh food wasted.
+
+## Delivery
+
+The [reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends the member a reminder of their pickup slot the day
+before. It uses SMS to the member's phone number.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, the pantry tried email reminders. The provider's report showed that 34% of reminder emails
+were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup left a packed bag, with
+its fresh food going in the bin by closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone within
+the family and never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+
+In [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), volunteers proposed email again because SMS cost €40 a month and email was
+free. The maintainer kept SMS: the saving did not justify repeating the missed pickups and food waste seen during
+the trial. SMS retains that recurring cost in exchange for reaching members through a channel they see. Future
+proposals to change the channel need to address that experience, as well as the sending cost.
